<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83515" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλαστός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>formed, moulded</i>, esp. in clay or wax, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					513
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π. ὃ δὴ σκεῦος ὠνομάκαμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Sph.</u>
					219a
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐκ γαίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					52.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. εἰκών</span>
			<i>statue</i>, opp. painting, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ages.</u>
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>that can easily be moulded, plastic</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				386a27
			</span></i> ; <i>in a thick paste</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.4.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>fabricated, forged, counterfeit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ λόγου πλαστοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.68
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. βακχεῖαι</span>
			<i>sham</i> inspirations, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				218
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὴν φιλίαν παρέχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ages.</u>
					1.38
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλαστὸς πατρί</span> a
				<i>supposititious</i> son, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				780
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sosith.
				2.4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐπιχείρημα</span>
			<i>hypothetical</i> case, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Inv.</u>
				3.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				15
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶς</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄντως</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				216c
			</span></i> ; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀληθῶς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				642d
			</span></i> ; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύσει</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				777d
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὀδυρόμενοι</span>
			<i>feignedly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.381
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατός</span>
			.</div>
